---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import { company, site, power, network } from '../data/site';

const totalSqft = site.buildings.reduce((n, b) => n + b.sqft, 0);
---

<Content
  title={`${site.designation} — ${site.name} | ${company.full}`}
  description={`${site.acres} acres in ${site.county}, Oklahoma, owned outright, with three ${site.buildings[0].sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft buildings and an existing ${power.transformer} service already on the parcel. Power-on ${site.powerOn}.`}
  kicker={`${site.designation} · ${site.county}, Oklahoma`}
  heading="Forty acres that already have power on them."
  lede={`${site.address}. ${site.acres} acres, ${site.ownership.toLowerCase()}, three buildings standing, and a ${power.transformer} service energised on the parcel. Nothing here is optioned, leased or subject to a land assembly.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Parcel', value: `${site.acres} acres`, note: `${site.ownership}, ${site.county}`, count: true },
    { label: 'Buildings', value: `${totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft`, note: `${site.buildings.length} × ${site.buildings[0].sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft, standing`, count: true },
    { label: 'Electrical service', value: power.transformer, note: `${power.voltage}, energised on site`, tone: 'gold' },
    { label: 'Power-on target', value: site.powerOn, note: 'Phase 1A compute hall', tone: 'signal' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="today" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">On the ground</span></p>
    <h2 id="today">What exists today, not what is planned</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>
          Most AI data center sites are sold on a rendering and a land option.
          {' '}{company.name} owns the {site.acres} acres at {site.address} outright,
          the three buildings are already up, the {power.transformer} transformer is
          already set, and the fibre is a signed quote rather than a feasibility study.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          That changes what a tenant is underwriting. You are not underwriting whether
          the power will arrive, or whether the seller closes on the land. You are
          underwriting a fit-out schedule inside a building that exists.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      <p>This one is sold on a deed.</p>
      <p>
        {site.acres} acres at {site.address}. {site.ownership} in {site.county} —
        not optioned, not leased, not subject to a land assembly.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="land" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The land</span></p>
    <h2 id="land">The parcel</h2>

    <div class="split">
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Address</dt><dd>{site.address}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>County</dt><dd>{site.county}, Oklahoma</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Acreage</dt><dd>{site.acres} acres</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tenure</dt><dd>{site.ownership}<span class="note">No ground lease, no option, no assembly risk.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Frontage</dt><dd>US-70<span class="note">Highway frontage at the address above — the parcel is reached directly from the state highway, not from a county section road.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Parcel ID</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Bryan County assessor parcel number and legal description]</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Zoning</dt><dd><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: zoning classification and whether a data center is permitted by right]</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Utilities on parcel</dt><dd>Electrical service and fibre confirmed. <span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: water source, sanitary/septic, and natural gas availability]</span></dd></div>
      </dl>

      <figure class="photo">
        <div class="photo__frame">
          <svg class="photo__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="14" rx="2" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3.5" />
            <path d="M8.5 6l1.4-2.2h4.2L15.5 6" />
            <path d="M3 3l18 18" />
          </svg>
          <p class="photo__state">Photograph not taken yet</p>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <b>[PHOTO NEEDED]</b> Aerial of the full {site.acres}-acre parcel with the three
          buildings and the US-70 frontage visible, ideally flown in daylight with the
          boundary legible. Company policy is a real photograph or an empty frame — no
          stock, no render.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="buildings" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">The buildings</span></p>
    <h2 id="buildings">Three shells, phased</h2>

    <p>
      The three buildings are identical {site.buildings[0].sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft
      shells. Phase 1A takes the first one. The other two stay as expansion shells so a
      second and third deployment do not wait on new construction, only on fit-out.
    </p>

    <div class="scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Building schedule, scrollable">
      <table>
        <caption>Building schedule, Site 01</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Building</th>
            <th scope="col">Footprint</th>
            <th scope="col">Role</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.buildings.map((b) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Building {b.id}</th>
              <td class="num">{b.sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft</td>
              <td>{b.role}</td>
              <td>
                {b.id === 1
                  ? `Fit-out for ${site.powerOn} power-on`
                  : 'Shell, available for fit-out'}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Total</th>
            <td class="num">{totalSqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft</td>
            <td>Across {site.buildings.length} buildings</td>
            <td><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: clear height, slab loading, and roof structure per building]</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top: var(--s-5);">
      Structural and mechanical detail a tenant will ask for before signing —
      clear height, floor loading in lbs/sq ft, door and equipment access,
      and the route for liquid cooling pipework — is
      {' '}<span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: as-built drawings and structural report for Buildings 1–3]</span>.
      We would rather show you nothing than a number we have not measured.
    </p>

    <figure class="photo" style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      <div class="photo__frame">
        <svg class="photo__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" aria-hidden="true">
          <rect x="2.5" y="6" width="19" height="14" rx="2" />
          <circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3.5" />
          <path d="M8.5 6l1.4-2.2h4.2L15.5 6" />
          <path d="M3 3l18 18" />
        </svg>
        <p class="photo__state">Photograph not taken yet</p>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <b>[PHOTO NEEDED]</b> Ground-level exterior of Building 1 and, separately, the
        empty interior of Building 1 before fit-out. The empty interior is the more
        persuasive image: it is the thing a tenant is buying.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="why" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">04</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Location</span></p>
    <h2 id="why">Why Mead</h2>

    <p>
      The location argument is not about a metro or a fibre hub. It is about what was
      already sitting on this parcel when we bought it.
    </p>

    <div class="cards">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The service was already there</h3>
        <p>
          A {power.transformer} service at {power.voltage} is standing and energised on
          the parcel. A new large-load request would put a site in an interconnection
          queue that currently runs {power.industryQueue}. This one is not in that queue.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The buildings were already there</h3>
        <p>
          {site.buildings.length} × {site.buildings[0].sqft.toLocaleString()} sq ft of
          existing shell removes ground-up construction from the critical path. Phase 1A
          is a fit-out, not a build.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The land is owned, not optioned</h3>
        <p>
          {site.ownership} in {site.county}. There is no landowner to renegotiate with
          and no option to exercise before a tenant can be given a term sheet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The fibre is quoted, not scoped</h3>
        <p>
          {network.speed} from {network.provider} on a {network.term.toLowerCase()}.
          Rural Oklahoma is often written off on connectivity; this parcel is not.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="diligence" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">05</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Diligence</span></p>
    <h2 id="diligence">What we have not published yet</h2>

    <p>
      Anything below is a real diligence item a tenant or lender will ask for. We have
      not published a number because we do not yet have one we would stand behind. This
      list is here so you can ask for the ones that matter to you rather than discover
      the gap in week six.
    </p>

    <ul class="bullets">
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: ALTA survey and title commitment]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: FEMA flood zone determination for the parcel]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Phase I environmental site assessment]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: geotechnical report — bearing capacity for equipment pads and the solar array]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: seismic and wind design criteria used for Buildings 1–3]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: water availability and volume, and whether any cooling loop needs it]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: Bryan County and Oklahoma tax treatment applicable to the site]</span></li>
      <li><span class="todo">[PLACEHOLDER: nearest commercial airport and drive time for hands-on site visits]</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="next" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">06</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Next</span></p>
    <h2 id="next">The power is the reason this site is worth reading about</h2>
    <p>
      Thirty owned acres is a good starting position. It is the electrical position that
      makes the schedule real: an existing service, {power.headroom}, and no
      interconnection application to file.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/power">Read the power story</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact">Arrange a site visit</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
